      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 79: 🔴 `onRestoreFile` returns early for unsupported types, `restoreFailed`, and non-allowlisted destinations without consuming the current entry payload. In Android full-restore, each callback is positioned on that entry’s data; if bytes are not drained/skipped, subsequent entries can be misaligned or corrupted. Always consume `size` bytes even when rejecting an entry (e.g., call `FullBackup.restoreFile(data, size, type, mode, mtime, null)` or explicitly read/discard the stream before returning).",
